---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import More from "../../components/More.astro";
import Overview from "../../components/Overview.astro";
import { getSnapshot, coldStart } from "../../lib/hyperliquid.ts";
import { usd, pct } from "../../lib/funding.ts";
import { readFundingPaid, HL_BASE_HOURLY } from "../../lib/funding-paid.ts";
import { shortDate, plural } from "../../../public/shared.js";

/* WHAT A FUNDING RATE COST, IN DOLLARS, ACROSS THE BOOK. See src/lib/funding-paid.ts for the
   method and every approximation in it. This page is the one place on the site that prints the
   sum, and it is built to be quoted: one figure, its window, its population and its method. */
const env = (Astro.locals as any)?.runtime?.env;
const snap = await getSnapshot(env?.SNAPSHOT, import.meta.env.DEV);
if (!snap.available) return coldStart();
const read = await readFundingPaid(env?.DB, env?.SNAPSHOT, Date.now(), 30, import.meta.env.DEV);
/* NO PAGE WITHOUT THE FIGURE. A page whose whole content is one sum does not render an empty
   version of itself; it answers 503 like every page here whose store is cold. */
if (read.status !== "ready") return coldStart();
const paid = read.paid;

const live = new Set(snap.perps.map((p) => p.symbol));
const premium = paid.net - paid.base;
const baseShare = paid.base / paid.net;
const top = paid.rows[0];
const days = Math.round(paid.span / 24);
const asOf = shortDate(paid.last);
const retired = paid.rows.filter((r) => !live.has(r.symbol)).length;
const baseHourPct = paid.hours ? paid.baseHours / paid.hours : NaN;
const ratePct = pct(HL_BASE_HOURLY, 5);

const title = "Funding paid on Hyperliquid: what longs paid shorts in 30 days";
const description = `Over the ${days} days to ${asOf}, longs paid shorts a net ${usd(paid.net)} in funding on Hyperliquid across ${paid.rows.length} contracts; ${usd(paid.base)} of it is the fixed base rate. Per contract, from settled hourly rates and hourly open interest.`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description} fetchedAt={paid.last} crumb={{ href: "/funding", label: "Funding", current: "Funding paid" }}>
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/funding">Funding</a> › Funding paid</p>
    <h1>Funding paid on Hyperliquid</h1>
    <Overview>
      {paid.net >= 0
        ? <>Over the {days} days to {asOf}, <b>longs paid shorts a net {usd(paid.net)}</b> in funding on Hyperliquid, across {paid.rows.length} contracts.</>
        : <>Over the {days} days to {asOf}, <b>shorts paid longs a net {usd(-paid.net)}</b> in funding on Hyperliquid, across {paid.rows.length} contracts.</>}
      {" "}<b>{usd(paid.base)}</b> of it is the fixed base rate of {ratePct} an hour{paid.net > 0 && <> &mdash; {pct(baseShare, 1)} of the total</>}, and the market premium added {premium >= 0 ? usd(premium) : <>&minus;{usd(-premium)}</>} on top.
      {" "}{pct(baseHourPct, 1)} of contract-hours settled at exactly that rate. The most was paid on <b>{top.symbol}</b>, {usd(top.longsPaid + top.shortsPaid)} changing hands.
    </Overview>
    <p>
      Hyperliquid&rsquo;s funding rate is the premium plus a clamped interest term fixed at 0.01% per
      eight hours. While the premium stays inside the clamp, which is most hours, the rate is that
      interest term and nothing else, paid hourly at one eighth: a charge longs pay shorts for
      holding the position, whatever the market is doing.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="panel"><table class="tbl paidtbl" data-sortable>
    <thead><tr><th>Coin</th><th class="num">Longs paid shorts</th><th class="num">Shorts paid longs</th><th class="num">Net</th><th class="num">At base rate <span class="thscope">share of hours</span></th><th class="num">Hours held <span class="thscope">of {paid.span}</span></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {paid.rows.map((r) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{live.has(r.symbol) ? <a href={`/funding/${r.symbol.toLowerCase()}`}>{r.symbol}</a> : <>{r.symbol}{" "}<span class="faint">no longer covered</span></>}</td>
          <td>{usd(r.longsPaid)}</td>
          <td>{usd(r.shortsPaid)}</td>
          <td class={r.net >= 0 ? "pays-l" : "pays-s"}>{r.net >= 0 ? usd(r.net) : <>&minus;{usd(-r.net)}</>}</td>
          <td>{pct(r.baseHours / r.hours, 0)}</td>
          <td>{r.hours}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="section-note" style="margin:12px 0 20px;max-width:74ch">
    Net is amber where longs paid on balance and cyan where shorts did. Listed: every contract with
    both an open-interest reading and a settled rate in the window, {paid.rows.length} in all{retired > 0 && <>, {plural(retired, "of which has", "of which have")} since fallen below the coverage floor</>}.
    {paid.unjoined.length > 0 && <>{" "}Left out: {paid.unjoined.join(", ")}, which had open interest recorded here but no stored funding history to multiply it by.</>}
    An hour counts only where both an open-interest reading and a settled rate are held; the last
    column is how many did, out of the {paid.span} in the window.
  </p>

  <More label="How the figure is built, and what it approximates">
    <p>
      Hyperliquid charges <code>position_size × oracle_price × funding_rate</code> every hour. Summed
      over every position, position size is open interest: each long has a short on the other side,
      so open interest is one side&rsquo;s size, and what one side pays the other receives. Each
      hour here is open interest, read on the first minute of that hour, times the rate Hyperliquid
      settled for it, from its own funding history.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two approximations, both small. Open interest is valued at the mark price where the payment
      uses the oracle price; they differ by the premium, a fraction of a percent outside a
      dislocation. And an hour with either reading missing is left out rather than filled in, which
      makes every figure a floor: the table prints the hours each one is built from.
    </p>
    <p>
      The window is this site&rsquo;s open-interest store, kept hourly since 16 September 2026 and
      for 30 days. It covers the contracts on this site, each holding at least the open-interest
      floor named on <a class="link" href="/about">About</a>, not every market Hyperliquid lists.
      {" "}<a class="link" href="/data-sources">Where each series comes from →</a>
    </p>
  </More>

  <p style="margin:20px 0 0">
    <a class="link" href="/funding">Funding rates on every contract →</a>{" "}
    <a class="link" href="/funding/history">What funding took from a long over seven months →</a>{" "}
    <a class="link" href="/learn/funding-rate">What a funding rate is, and who pays it →</a>
  </p>
  <style is:global>
    .paidtbl td + td { font-family: var(--mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
  </style>
</Base>
